{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong></strong><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras/2f0731a0a508e93c78128d8cda091194.poster.avif?t=1768630646\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras/2f0731a0a508e93c78128d8cda091194.webm?t=1768630646\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras/2f0731a0a508e93c78128d8cda091194.mp4?t=1768630646\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Eternal Afternoon</strong> is a poetic walking sim about wasting time before the end of the world. You play as Sasha, a 10-year-old boy wandering his neighborhood in the final minutes before a giant black wave swallows everything.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras/1d4ff12ced06586ea2b80dfe56b30705.avif?t=1768630646\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras_big/1d4ff12ced06586ea2b80dfe56b30705.webp?t=1768630646 width=1560 height=128 /></span></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Retro nostalgic visuals &amp; authentic atmosphere</strong> \u2013 a suburban block in the summer of 2001, recreated with care. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A chilling meditation on time, death, and the inevitable</strong> \u2013 experience the quiet dread of a world that ends in twenty minutes. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Story through exploration</strong> \u2013 uncover small moments, side quests, and fragments of mystery woven into the neighborhood. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Built with replayability and speedrun in mind</strong> \u2013 no save system, no upgrades; your only progress is knowledge of how the world works and how everything connects.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3924170?t=1768630646","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/78ae44854ee403068ac312a06a45449b7076a781/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1768630646","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/e4bc63b4e4880ff19073b35644cf4f38685377af/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1768630646","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/e4bc63b4e4880ff19073b35644cf4f38685377af/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1768630646","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Steam Achievements","id":22},{"description":"Full controller support","id":28},{"description":"Custom Volume Controls","id":68},{"description":"Playable without Timed Input","id":74},{"description":"Stereo Sound","id":69},{"description":"Surround Sound","id":70},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[5],"notes":"The game deals with complex issues related to the perception of time, death, and video games as a way of self-expression. The game also contains certain moments that may be psychologically frightening for children. The game is *not* recommended for children! Its target audience is adults looking for an authentic, nostalgic and unique experience in the ganre of walking simulators."},"controller_support":"full","detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong></strong><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras/2f0731a0a508e93c78128d8cda091194.poster.avif?t=1768630646\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras/2f0731a0a508e93c78128d8cda091194.webm?t=1768630646\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras/2f0731a0a508e93c78128d8cda091194.mp4?t=1768630646\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Eternal Afternoon</strong> is a poetic walking sim about wasting time before the end of the world. You play as Sasha, a 10-year-old boy wandering his neighborhood in the final minutes before a giant black wave swallows everything.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras/1d4ff12ced06586ea2b80dfe56b30705.avif?t=1768630646\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3924170/extras_big/1d4ff12ced06586ea2b80dfe56b30705.webp?t=1768630646 width=1560 height=128 /></span></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Retro nostalgic visuals &amp; authentic atmosphere</strong> \u2013 a suburban block in the summer of 2001, recreated with care. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A chilling meditation on time, death, and the inevitable</strong> \u2013 experience the quiet dread of a world that ends in twenty minutes. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Story through exploration</strong> \u2013 uncover small moments, side quests, and fragments of mystery woven into the neighborhood. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Built with replayability and speedrun in mind</strong> \u2013 no save system, no upgrades; your only progress is knowledge of how the world works and how everything connects.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>","developers":["Alex Klexber"],"genres":[{"description":"Adventure","id